# FA3 Persistent + Varlen Tile Scheduler — Mechanism Report

Reference root: `/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/`

**vLLM fork note:** `VARLEN_ONLY` + `PACKGQA_ONLY` are enabled; `varlen_sort_batches = false` and launch-template `Sort = false`, so batch LPT-sort is compiled but inactive in this build.

---

## 1. Scheduler Variants and Selection

Selection happens at **compile time** in `flash_fwd_launch_template.h` via two nested `std::conditional_t`s.

### Type aliases

```61:78:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
    static constexpr int NumProducerThreads = Arch >= 90 ? CollectiveMainloop::NumProducerThreads : CollectiveMainloop::NumMmaThreads;
    static constexpr bool LPT = Is_causal || Is_local;
    // static constexpr bool Sort = !Is_local;
     static constexpr bool Sort = false;
    using SchedulerPersistent = std::conditional_t<Varlen,
        flash::VarlenDynamicPersistentTileScheduler<kBlockM, kBlockN, CollectiveMainloop::NumMmaThreads, NumProducerThreads, Split, PackGQA, Arch >= 90 /*WarpSpecialized*/, LPT, Sort, true /*Prepared*/>,
        std::conditional_t<!Is_causal && !Is_local,
            flash::StaticPersistentTileScheduler<Split>,
            flash::DynamicPersistentTileScheduler<CollectiveMainloop::NumMmaThreads, NumProducerThreads, Split, PackGQA, Arch >= 90 /*WarpSpecialized*/>
        >
    >;
    using SchedulerSingleTile = flash::SingleTileScheduler<Varlen, Split, PackGQA, kBlockM>;
    // If Split then we probably don't have enough work for PersistentScheduler to be useful.
    // However, if Varlen (e.g., during decode where we have max_seqlens), using PersistentScheduler is better
    // since we'll avoid launching a bunch of thread blocks that immediately exit.
    // On Sm80, noncausal persistent seems a bit slower.
    static constexpr bool UsePersistentScheduler = Arch >= 90 ? !(Split && !Varlen) : ((Is_causal && !Varlen) || (Varlen && Split));
    using Scheduler = std::conditional_t<!UsePersistentScheduler, SchedulerSingleTile, SchedulerPersistent>;
```

### Decision table (SM90 / Hopper — your port target)

| Condition | Scheduler | Mechanism |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|
| `Split && !Varlen` | `SingleTileScheduler` | 1 CTA per tile; grid = `(m_block, split×head, batch)` |
| `Varlen` (any split) | `VarlenDynamicPersistentTileScheduler` | `num_sm` CTAs + atomic work queue + prep metadata |
| `!Varlen && !Is_causal && !Is_local` | `StaticPersistentTileScheduler` | `num_sm` CTAs, strided `tile_idx += gridDim.x` (no atomic) |
| `!Varlen && (Is_causal \|\| Is_local)` | `DynamicPersistentTileScheduler` | `num_sm` CTAs + atomic + L2 swizzle + LPT |

**Compile-time knobs:**
- `Varlen` — from `VARLEN_SWITCH` (cu_seqlens / seqused / leftpad)
- `Split` — kernel instantiation flag (`Split` template param)
- `Is_causal`, `Is_local` — from params
- `LPT = Is_causal || Is_local` — passed into varlen scheduler
- `Sort = false` in vLLM fork (would enable batch reordering in prep kernel)
- `Prepared = true` — varlen scheduler reads precomputed `prepare_seqlen_q_ptr` etc.

### Host-side: when is the atomic semaphore allocated?

In `mha_fwd` (not identical to `get_scheduler_metadata`):

```1049:1052:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_api.cpp
    // We don't use the persistent scheduler if Split and not Varlen
    bool const scheduler_needs_semaphore = params.arch >= 90
        ? (((params.is_causal || params.is_local) && (params.num_splits == 1)) || is_varlen)
        : ((params.is_causal && !is_varlen) || (is_varlen && params.num_splits > 1));
```

On SM90, semaphore is needed for: **varlen always**, or **causal/local with `num_splits==1`**. Dense bidirectional (`!causal && !local && !varlen`) uses `StaticPersistentTileScheduler` which does **not** use the semaphore.

`get_scheduler_metadata` is more conservative: `scheduler_needs_semaphore = (arch >= 90) || (num_splits > 1)`.

---

## 2. Persistent Grid Sizing and CTA Loop

### Grid dimensions

All persistent schedulers return **`grid = {num_sm, 1, 1}`**:

```167:170:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
    static dim3
    get_grid_shape(Params const& params, int num_sm) {
        return {uint32_t(num_sm)};
    }
```

(Same pattern at lines 279–281, 423–425 for Dynamic/Varlen.)

`num_sm` comes from device properties minus `sm_margin`:

```151:173:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
        int sm_count = args.hw_info.sm_count;
        if (sm_count <= 0) {
            ...
            sm_count = cutlass::KernelHardwareInfo::query_device_multiprocessor_count(args.hw_info.device_id);
        }
        ...
        return TileScheduler::get_grid_shape(params.scheduler, params.hw_info.sm_count);
```

**Interpretation:** exactly **one CTA per SM** (not multiple waves of CTAs). Each CTA loops until no valid work remains.

### Producer persistent loop (SM90 kernel)

```337:373:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
            cutlass::arch::wait_on_dependent_grids();

            // Load Q, K, V
            for (auto work_tile_info = SingleProducerWarp || warp_idx_in_warpgroup == 0 ? scheduler.template get_initial_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/true>(params.scheduler) : scheduler.template get_initial_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler);
                 work_tile_info.is_valid(params.scheduler);
                 work_tile_info = SingleProducerWarp || warp_idx_in_warpgroup == 0 ? scheduler.template get_next_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/true>(params.scheduler, work_tile_info) : scheduler.template get_next_work</*IsProducerWarp=*/false>(params.scheduler, work_tile_info)) {

                auto block_coord = work_tile_info.get_block_coord(params.scheduler);
                ...
                auto scheduler_prefetch = [&scheduler, &params, &work_tile_info]() {
                    scheduler.prefetch_next_work(params.scheduler, work_tile_info);
                };
                mainloop.load(..., scheduler_prefetch, seqlen_info, block_coord, work_idx);
            }
```

Consumer loop (get_next_work called before epilogue, after MMA):

```391:467:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
