## 3. DynamicPersistent: Atomic Handout and Load Balancing

### Semaphore protocol

Only **one thread per producer group** (thread 0 of each producer sub-group) does the atomic:

```336:362:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
    prefetch_next_work(Params const& params, WorkTileInfo& current_work) const {
        if (threadIdx.x % NumProducerThreads == 0) {
            current_work.tile_idx = atomicAdd(params.tile_count_semaphore, 1) + int(gridDim.x);
        }
    }
    ...
    get_next_work(Params const& params, WorkTileInfo const& current_work) const {
        if constexpr (IsProducerWarp) {
            int new_tile_idx = __shfl_sync(0xffffffff, current_work.tile_idx, 0 /*lane*/);
            flash::named_barrier_sync(NumThreads, ...StreamkBarrier0...);
            if (threadIdx.x % NumProducerThreads == 0) {
                *tile_count_smem = current_work.tile_idx;
            }
            flash::named_barrier_arrive(NumThreads, ...StreamkBarrier1...);
            return {new_tile_idx};
        } else {
            flash::named_barrier_sync(NumThreads, ...StreamkBarrier1...);
            int tile_idx = *tile_count_smem;
            flash::named_barrier_arrive(NumThreads, ...StreamkBarrier0...);
            return {tile_idx};
        }
    }
```

**Mechanism:**
1. CTA `blockIdx.x` starts with tile `blockIdx.x` (`get_initial_work`).
2. While processing tile `t`, producer prefetches: `next = atomicAdd(semaphore, 1) + gridDim.x`.
3. Standard persistent pattern: CTAs `0..num_sm-1` take tiles `0..num_sm-1`; the atomic counter starts at 0, so the first `atomicAdd` returns 0 and CTA 0's second tile is `0 + num_sm = num_sm`.
4. Producer broadcasts `next` to MMA warps via named barriers + 1-word smem (`tile_count_smem`).

This is **CUDA `atomicAdd` on global `int*`** — not custom PTX `red.global`. You can use `atomicAdd(semaphore, 1)` directly.

**Semaphore init:**
- Host: `tile_count_semaphore.zero_()` when not varlen (`flash_api.cpp:1078`)
- Prep kernel: `*tile_count_semaphore = 0` (`flash_prepare_scheduler.cu:77`)

### L2 swizzling + LPT (Dynamic dense causal)

Comment at top of class:

```226:233:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
    // This scheduler targets the causal (or local) case where each tile takes different
    // amount of time. We use longest-processing-time-first scheduling:
    // the longest remaining tile is assigned to the first SM that's free.
    // SM indicates they are free by incrementing a semaphore.
    // However, we have to make sure K & V still fit into L2 cache, so we perform scheduling
    // on "sections" of the head & batch dimension, each section consisting of e.g. 8 heads.
```

**L2 section size** (host-side in `to_underlying_arguments`):

```257:276:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
        int const size_one_kv_head = args.seqlen_k * (args.headdim + args.headdim_v) * args.element_size * 2;
        int const size_l2 = 32 * 1024 * 1024;  // 32 MB for K & V
        int const swizzle = (size_l2 < size_one_kv_head ? 1 : (1 << cutlass::find_log2(size_l2 / size_one_kv_head))) * (PackGQA ? 1 : args.qhead_per_khead);
        ...
        int const num_split_blocks = args.num_blocks * (!Split ? 1 : args.num_splits);
        return {num_split_blocks * args.num_head * args.num_batch,
                cutlass::FastDivmod(args.num_blocks), cutlass::FastDivmod(args.num_head),
                cutlass::FastDivmod(swizzle), cutlass::FastDivmod(swizzle * num_split_blocks),
                cutlass::FastDivmod(num_hb_remainder > 0 ? num_hb_remainder : 1),
                (args.num_head * args.num_batch) / swizzle,
                args.tile_count_semaphore};
```

**LPT reversal** (process large `m_block` first — causal tiles get cheaper toward `m_block=0`):

```311:313:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
            // Longest-processing-time-first
            block = params.m_block_divmod.divisor - 1 - block;
            return {block, bidh, bidb, split_idx};
```

**Load balancing:** dynamic atomic assignment means the next free SM always grabs the next global tile index. Combined with LPT tile ordering, long tiles are issued first; fast CTAs pull more work from the queue.

