## 4. VarlenDynamicPersistent: Prep Kernel, Tile Mapping, Ordering

### Prep kernel launch geometry

```214:249:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
void prepare_varlen_num_blocks(Flash_fwd_params &params, cudaStream_t stream, bool packgqa,
                               int blockM, int blockN, bool enable_pdl) {
    int qhead_per_khead = cutlass::ceil_div(params.h, params.h_k);
    int num_warps = cutlass::ceil_div(params.b, 31); // warp switch will cap this at 32
    int num_ctas = cutlass::ceil_div(params.b, 31 * 32);
    ...
    int const max_kvblocks_in_l2 = size_l2 / size_one_kvblock;
    BOOL_SWITCH(params.varlen_sort_batches, Sort, [&] {
        NUM_WARP_SWITCH(num_warps, NumWarps, [&] {
            flash::prepare_varlen_num_blocks_kernel<NumWarps, Sort><<<num_ctas /*grid*/, 32 * NumWarps /*block*/, 0, stream>>>(
                ...
                params.tile_count_semaphore,
                params.prepare_seqlen_q_ptr,
                params.num_splits_dynamic_ptr,
                params.varlen_batch_idx_ptr,
                params.num_nheads_in_l2_ptr,
                ...);
        });
    });
}
```

- Each warp covers **31 batches** (lanes 0–30; lane 31 is sentinel in sort path).
- Max **992 batches** (`31×32`) in one prep CTA → `PREPARE_VARLEN_MAX_BATCHES_1CTA`.
- If `b > 992`: split-KV disabled (`flash_api.cpp:1045`).

### Per-batch computation in prep kernel

**M blocks + seqlen_q:**

```81:95:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    auto get_num_m_blocks_and_seqlen = [&](int batch_idx) {
        ...
        return batch_idx < num_batch && lane < kNumBatchPerWarp
            ? cute::make_tuple(blockm_divmod.div(seqlen * (packgqa ? qhead_per_khead : 1) + blockm_divmod.divisor - 1), seqlen)
            : cute::make_tuple(0, 0);
    };
```

(`blockm_divmod.div(x)` = `⌈x / kBlockM⌉` using precomputed ceiling div.)

**N blocks (for split heuristic + sort key):**

```97:121:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    auto get_num_n_blocks = [&](int batch_idx) {
        ...
        seqlen = seqlen - leftpad_k + seqlen_new;
        return batch_idx < num_batch && lane < kNumBatchPerWarp
            ? blockn_divmod.div(seqlen + blockn_divmod.divisor - 1) : 0;
    };
```

**Dynamic split count** (only when single prep CTA and `num_splits_static > 1`):

```143:164:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    if (int(gridDim.x) > 1 || num_splits_static == 1) {
        num_splits_dynamic = 1;
    } else {
        int total_blocks = num_m_blocks * num_n_blocks;
        // Warp sum
        for (int i = cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp / 2; i >= 1; i /= 2) {
            total_blocks += __shfl_down_sync(0xffffffff, total_blocks, i);
        }
        if (lane == 0) { atomicAdd(total_blocks_smem, total_blocks); }
        __syncthreads();
        total_blocks = total_blocks_smem[0];
        // 10% margin
        int blocks_per_sm = static_cast<int>(ceilf(float(total_blocks) * 1.1f * float(num_head) / float(num_sm)));
        num_splits_dynamic = std::max(std::min((num_n_blocks + blocks_per_sm - 1) / blocks_per_sm, num_splits_static), 1);
        num_n_blocks = cutlass::ceil_div(num_n_blocks, num_splits_dynamic); 
    }
```

**L2 head swizzle count** (stored per batch):

```133:141:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    auto get_nheads_in_l2 = [&](int n_blocks) {
        int nheads_in_l2 = n_blocks * 16 <= max_kvblocks_in_l2 ? 16
            : n_blocks * 8 <= max_kvblocks_in_l2 ? 8
            : n_blocks * 4 <= max_kvblocks_in_l2 ? 4
            : n_blocks * 2 <= max_kvblocks_in_l2 ? 2
            : 1;
        if(!packgqa) { nheads_in_l2 *= qhead_per_khead; }
        return min(nheads_in_l2, num_head);
    };
```

**Non-sort output path** (active in vLLM fork):

```201:207:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    } else {
        if (batch_idx < num_batch && lane < kNumBatchPerWarp) {
            prepare_seqlen_q_ptr[batch_idx] = seqlen_q * (packgqa ? qhead_per_khead : 1);
            if(num_splits_dynamic_ptr) { num_splits_dynamic_ptr[batch_idx] = num_splits_dynamic; }
            if(num_nheads_in_l2_ptr) { num_nheads_in_l2_ptr[batch_idx] = get_nheads_in_l2(max(num_n_blocks, 1)); }
        }
    }
```

**Sort path** (compiled, disabled in vLLM): descending sort on adjusted `num_n_blocks` key; causal adjusts key by `seqlen_q/2` so longer causal work sorts first:

```166:199:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_prepare_scheduler.cu
    if constexpr (Sort) {
        ...
        else if (is_causal) {
            num_n_blocks = num_n_blocks * blockn_divmod.divisor - (seqlen_q / 2);
        }
        int4 batch_coords[ITEMS_PER_THREAD];
        batch_coords[0] = make_int4(num_n_blocks, seqlen_q, num_splits_dynamic, batch_idx);
        BlockMergeSort(temp_storage).Sort(batch_coords, PrepareSortOp<int4>());
        ...
        prepare_seqlen_q_ptr[batch_idx] = batch_coords[0].y * (packgqa ? qhead_per_khead : 1);
        num_splits_dynamic_ptr[batch_idx] = batch_coords[0].z;
        varlen_batch_idx_ptr[batch_idx] = batch_coords[0].w;
    }
```

Uses **CUB BlockMergeSort** — the heaviest CUTLASS/CUB dependency in the prep path.

### Varlen tile index → (batch, head, m_block, split)

Core function: `tile_idx_to_work_tile`. Global linear index space:

For batch `b`: **`num_head × num_m_blocks × num_splits`** tiles (splits=1 if !Split).

**Batch lookup** — warp scans 31 batches at a time using prefix sums:

```511:559:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
        int num_m_blocks = get_num_m_blocks(current_work.bidb);
        int num_splits = get_num_splits(current_work.bidb);
        int num_split_m_blocks = !Split ? num_m_blocks : num_m_blocks * num_splits;
        int num_m_blocks_cumulative = warp_prefix_sum(num_split_m_blocks);
        int m_blocks_in_group = __shfl_sync(0xffffffff, num_m_blocks_cumulative, cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp - 1);
        int group_end_tile = current_work.tile_idx + m_blocks_in_group * params.num_head;
        int bidb = current_work.bidb;
        while (group_end_tile <= next_tile_idx) {
            bidb += cutlass::NumThreadsPerWarp - 1;
            if (bidb >= params.num_batch) {
                return {next_tile_idx, 0, 0, params.num_batch};  // sentinel: done
            }
            ...
            group_end_tile += m_blocks_in_group * params.num_head;
        }
        ...
        int batch_idx_in_group = __popc(__ballot_sync(0xffffffff, group_start_tile + num_m_blocks_cumulative * params.num_head <= next_tile_idx));
        bidb += batch_idx_in_group;
        ...
        int mh_block = next_tile_idx - group_start_tile;
```

**Within-batch decode** (non-LPT or split>1):

```611:627:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
            bidh = mh_block / num_m_blocks;
            block = mh_block - bidh * num_m_blocks;
            if constexpr (Split) {
                int bidh_actual = bidh / num_splits;
                int split_idx = bidh - bidh_actual * num_splits;
                uint32_t bidh_packed = reinterpret_cast<uint32_t&>(bidh_actual) + (reinterpret_cast<uint32_t&>(split_idx) << 16) + (reinterpret_cast<uint32_t&>(num_splits) << 24);
                bidh = reinterpret_cast<int&>(bidh_packed);
            }
```

**LPT path** (`LPT=true`, `num_splits==1`): section by `nheads_in_l2`, reverse m_block:

```577:610:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
                int nheads_in_l2 = get_nheads_in_l2(bidb);
                int mh_in_l2 = nheads_in_l2 * num_m_blocks;
                int section_idx = mh_block / mh_in_l2;
                ...
                block = l2_mod / nheads_in_this_section;
                ...
                bidh = section_idx * nheads_in_l2 + bidh_residual;
                ...
            block = num_m_blocks - 1 - block;
```

**Virtual batch index** (when Sort+Prepared): `varlen_batch_idx_ptr[virtual_bidb]`.

**`get_block_coord` unpacks split from packed `bidh`:**

```448:464:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
            if constexpr (!Split) {
                return {block, bidh, get_actual_batch(bidb), 0 /*split_idx*/};
            } else {
                uint32_t bidh_packed = reinterpret_cast<uint32_t const&>(bidh);
                uint32_t bidh_actual_u = bidh_packed & 0x0000FFFF;
                int bidh_actual = reinterpret_cast<int&>(bidh_actual_u);
                uint32_t split_idx_u = ((bidh_packed & 0x00FF0000) >> 16) + ((bidh_packed & 0xFF000000) >> 8);
                int split_idx = reinterpret_cast<int&>(split_idx_u);
                return {block, bidh_actual, get_actual_batch(bidb), split_idx};
            }
```

Varlen uses the **same atomic semaphore** as Dynamic (`prefetch_next_work` / `get_next_work` at lines 657–686), but broadcasts **`int4`** `{group_start_tile, block, bidh, bidb}` through smem for consumers.

---

## 5. Split-KV and the Scheduler

### Work grid expansion

**Static/Dynamic dense:** `total_blocks = num_blocks × num_head × num_batch × num_splits`.

**Varlen:** no fixed `total_blocks`; each batch contributes `num_head × ceil_div(seqlen_q_packgqa, kBlockM) × num_splits_dynamic[b]`. Invalid/out-of-range tiles get sentinel `bidb = num_batch`.

**SingleTile (Split+!Varlen):** grid `{num_blocks, num_splits×num_head, batch}`; split extracted from `blockIdx.y`:

```104:108:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_scheduler.hpp
        if constexpr (Split) {
            int split_idx;
            work_info.bidh = params.nsplits_divmod.divmod(split_idx, work_info.bidh);
            work_info.split_idx = split_idx;
        }
```

Varlen SingleTile packs dynamic num_splits into high 16 bits of `split_idx` (`lines 117–122`).

### N-block range assignment (actual KV split — separate from scheduler)

